  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-purpose Cash Assistance for flood affected populations in Myanmar</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will provide multi-purpose cash assistance (MPCA) to flood-affected populations in Myanmar, enabling them to meet their most urgent needs. IOM will target vulnerable households who were affected by flooding caused by Typhoon Yagi in Mandalay, Bago (East), Shan (South and East) and Kayin. Working with partners, who have access to affected locations, and in line with the guidance of the Cash and Markets Working Group (CMWG), IOM will provide a one-off tranche of 310,000 MMK per affected household and will reach an estimated 55,040 individuals (19,462 women, 17,965 men, 9,159 girls, 8,454 boys).</narrative>
  </description>
